// Trader Moss — the shop interior's merchant. "Let's trade" hands off to the
// shop screen, so the conversation ends there.
//
// Also the demo for world flags (npc-dialogue-yarn.md Phase 3): the first visit
// sets met_shopkeeper, and every visit after that gets the returning-customer
// greeting instead — including after a save, quit and reload.
//
// And the demo for state queries (dialogue-state-conditions.md Phase 3): the
// under-the-counter medkit is offered only while the player can afford it, and
// once they have paid, Moss reads the balance they are left with. Both halves
// are the same feature from either side — what's in your pocket before you
// spend it, and after.

title: greet
---
<<if flag("met_shopkeeper")>>
    <<jump regular>>
<<else>>
    <<jump first_time>>
<<endif>>
===

title: first_time
---
<<set_flag met_shopkeeper>>
$npc: Welcome in. Best prices on the station — care to see my stock?
-> Let's trade
    <<open_shop>>
    <<stop>>
-> Anything under the counter? <<if credits() >= 150>>
    <<jump under_the_counter>>
-> Just looking
    <<jump just_looking>>
===

title: regular
---
<<play_anim Waving>>
$npc: Back again. Stock's turned over since you were last in — take a look.
-> Let's trade
    <<open_shop>>
    <<stop>>
-> Anything under the counter? <<if credits() >= 150>>
    <<jump under_the_counter>>
-> Just looking
    <<jump just_looking>>
===

// Gated on the price, so a player who can't pay never has the offer dangled in
// front of them — and the option is gone next visit if the medkit is what
// emptied their account.
title: under_the_counter
---
<<play_anim Use_Item>>
$npc: Surplus medkit. Hundred and fifty, and I never saw you.
-> Done
    <<credits -150>>
    <<give_item 4>>
    <<jump paid>>
-> Not at that price
    <<jump just_looking>>
===

// The other half: this router runs after the credits have left the account, so
// it sees what the purchase actually left behind (Phase 2 — a condition is read
// when the node is reached, not when the conversation starts).
title: paid
---
<<if credits() >= 150>>
    <<jump paid_flush>>
<<else>>
    <<jump paid_cleaned_out>>
<<endif>>
===

title: paid_flush
---
$npc: Pleasure doing business. There's more under here, if you're still buying.
===

title: paid_cleaned_out
---
$npc: Pleasure doing business. Come back when your credits have recovered.
===

title: just_looking
---
$npc: Take your time. Mind the merchandise.
===
